**b)** 
Use the normal approximation from a) and simulation to approximate the predictive distribution of the running time for a new Windows computer with performance measure equal to $1.3$.



::: {#q:expon_reg_approx_b .callout-note icon="false" collapse="true"}
## Solution


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
xPred = c(1, 1.3, 1)
yPredDraws = rep(0, nSim)
for (i in 1:nSim){
  yPredDraws[i] = rexp(1, 1/exp(xPred %*% betaDraws[i,]))
}
hist(yPredDraws, 30, freq = FALSE, main = "Predictive density", 
     xlab = "yPred", col = "cornsilk", xlim = c(0,20))
```

